# Walkthrough: User & Admin Architecture

## Overview
We have successfully refactored the application to support multiple users with distinct roles (**Admin** and **User**). The application now features a secure login screen and role-based dashboards.

## Credentials to Test
Use the following credentials to test the different roles:

### 1. Administrator
- **Cédula**: `1234567890`
- **Capabilities**:
  - View all registered users.
  - Assign loans and savings to users.
  - Edit store products (Price, Name, Category).

### 2. Regular User (Carlos Rodríguez)
- **Cédula**: `987654321`
- **Capabilities**:
  - View personal Dashboard (Savings, Loans).
  - Access the Store.
  - View personal Advisor.

## Key Changes

### 1. Login Screen
A new entry point for the application. It authenticates users based on their Cédula.
![Login Screen Mockup](https://via.placeholder.com/600x400/f1f5f9/0f172a?text=Login+Screen+Preview) 
*(Note: Actual screen matches the modern design style of the app)*

### 2. Admin Dashboard
When logging in as an Admin, you are taken to a specialized dashboard.
- **Usuarios Tab**: List of all users. Click "Asignar Préstamo" to interact (Logic ready for expansion).
- **Productos Tab**: Grid of store products. Click the "Edit" (Pencil) icon on a product to modify its details inline. Changes reflected instantly in the store.

### 3. Architecture Updates
- **[types.ts](file:///Users/javierportillarosero/Documents/PROG/fondof/types.ts)**: Added `Role` enum and [UserProfile](file:///Users/javierportillarosero/Documents/PROG/fondof/types.ts#45-57) extensions.
- **[constants.ts](file:///Users/javierportillarosero/Documents/PROG/fondof/constants.ts)**: Replaced single mock user with `MOCK_USERS` array.
- **[App.tsx](file:///Users/javierportillarosero/Documents/PROG/fondof/App.tsx)**: Implemented authentication flow and route protection.

## Next Steps
- Implement actual persistence for "Assign Loan" feature (currently just a UI button).
- Add "Create New User" functionality for Admins.
- Connect to a real backend.
